{"kind":"artifact","text":"First artifact at notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md, standing at exact clean head 1ad16e7ee87442b560712cc18de99627b3b662c3 on request/agents-md-cut. No live artifact covers this path, so there is no predecessor to retire — this is the first-artifact case, and the path is chosen to stay stable for whatever supersedes it later.\n\nThe file is 271 lines: a nine-line header giving the migration its context and pointing back at AGENTS.md, then 261 lines moved verbatim out of AGENTS.md lines 141 to 401. It carries the whole one-time whole-repository artifact migration: why an artifact at `.` is a silent omission that no future merge can ever supersede, the measurement that retiring the set flares roughly four fifths of the log at once, the six-step procedure with all five sh and jq programs unchanged, the quiet-wave precondition that no review request is awaiting its first verdict and no approved head is still out of main, and the closing gate that proves the migration finished by counting live artifacts at `.` and live artifacts still reaching one along artifact provenance.\n\nThe verbatim claim is proved mechanically, not by eye: diffing old AGENTS.md lines 141-401 against this file's lines 11-271 produces no output, and all five sh blocks are present and byte-identical. The jq is deliberately unchanged. A companion request, 7d38d1c9, asks for gs query capabilities that would let those programs become commands; when that lands, this file is the single place that needs rewriting, and that rewrite is a separate small child rather than part of either lane.\n\nWHY THIS MOVED AT ALL, which is the point of the change rather than a side effect. This runbook is a one-time operation that has never been executed, and it sat in the middle of the file every agent reads at the start of every session — about two thirds of AGENTS.md by line count. Worse, it carried its own numbered steps 1 to 6 inside a file whose work loop is numbered 1 to 7, so \"step 5\" named two different things in this repository and had already confused a reader. Moving it fixes the ambiguity and the attention cost in one act, and loses nothing, because the procedure is preserved exactly and AGENTS.md keeps a pointer paragraph naming the migration, its preconditions and its gate.\n\nGates at this exact head: make vet exit 0; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0 across 28 packages with no FAIL and no cached result; make docs ok in 47.3s; make build exit 0; gofmt -l . empty; git status --porcelain empty. The documentation citation gate walks docs/ only and this file is under notes/, so the gate does not reach it; that is stated rather than assumed, because a reader might expect otherwise given the file's citation-heavy content.\n\nThis artifact covers notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md. The companion artifact at AGENTS.md stands at this same head and must be co-signed with it, because the pointer in one and the content in the other are only true together.","body":{"commit":"1ad16e7ee87442b560712cc18de99627b3b662c3","path":"notes/retire-dot-artifacts.md"}}